  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1055 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nSaturday through Wednesday\n\nA 500 mb ridge will gradually build across the Upper Mississippi\nRiver Valley this weekend and remain in control of the region's\nweather through Wednesday. The weekend will be mainly sunny and\nthen as the ridge drifts further east it will become mostly to \npartly sunny. \n\nTemperatures will be near normal this weekend and then become \nabove-normal early next weekend. High temperatures are typically\nin the lower and mid-40s. Low temperatures typically range from\nthe mid-20s to around 30. \n\nThursday into Next Weekend\n\nTwo shortwave troughs will eject out of the western longwave\ntrough from Thursday into next weekend. The first one will \neject out on Wednesday night and Thursday. This system looks to \nstay well northwest of the region, so if we see any rainfall, it\nwill be likely very light on amounts. The second one will eject\nout next weekend. This one looks to be far enough southeast for\na better chance for appreciable rainfall. \n\nTemperatures will be well above-normal with high temperatures\nranging from the mid-50s to around 60 degrees (normals are\naround 40) and low temperatures will be in the 40s (normals are\nin the mid- to upper 20s).",
